    "q-125649": {
      "dom_id": "step-q125649",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14223200/assets/0f178c33254644c5e2e7bf6f3c596df87b1ea2f0b5bfd417c3f279f6c62b1b0d.png)\n\nConsider the circle $S$ and the vector field $F,$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the **clockwise** direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nII. ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n\nIII. ${∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$",
      "worked_solution": "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe now recall the following:\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves clockwise along $C.$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14223200/assets/f87d2e735ad58e0b33a813fb91ab202ac0eeaf90575979ea45f954fb7e1d0493.png)\n\nSo, $Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves counterclockwise along $C.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14223200/assets/102c11f9002e29a3759679c6ff0bd10188908d33eb9cc94a84d900956adc33a5.png)\n\nSo, $Γ={∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
