    "q-125424": {
      "dom_id": "step-q125424",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Consider the scalar field $f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $∇f$ is conservative\n\nII. ${∮}_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}$\n\nIII. ${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any piecewise smooth path $C\\in {R}^{2}$",
      "worked_solution": "If $F$ is a conservative vector field on ${R}^{2},$ then the circulation $Γ=0$ for any *closed* path $C\\in {R}^{2},$ that is \n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. The vector field $∇f$ is conservative by definition.\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. The result $Γ=0$ applies to closed curves only.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
